\f0\fs24 \cf0 I was approached in Hawaii to create a local pet products line brand.\
\
I wanted to approach this by using energetic primary colors in order to allude to the playfulness of children. I wanted this brand to speak to pet owners who view their own pets more than just a companion animal and as a part of their family and in many ways a furry four-legged child of their own.\
\
For this I worked with Aloha Gourmet to develop the brand name, Hana Paw. A play on the phrase Pau Hana, end of day, in Hawaii that is usually for after-work or school activities to have fun and relax. Hana Pa alludes to this inspiration while still having a meaning of its own. Directly translating to end-paw, or the last paw. I want to communicate to our audience that this was the last stop they needed for their furry-friend, they may have tried other pet goods but Hana Paw is the last one you\'92ll need to try since it focuses on real food, organic ingredients, and less chemicals in training pads and other products to truly give your pet the life they deserve, and act as sustainable as possible to protect animals for time to come.\
\
The branding for this chooses to be playful but clear in the messaging that this line makes happy, healthy, pets. Other products are still in production.}